<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirabeau B. Lamar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mirabeau Buonaparte Lamar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirabeau B. Lamar was a Georgia-born politician and soldier who was the second President of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, from 1838 to 1841. He fought at San Jacinto in 1836, moved the capital to the new city of Austin and promoted public education. His wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a>, heavy borrowing and the failed Santa Fe Expedition left the republic deeply in debt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirabeau-b-lamar.jpg" alt="Mirabeau B. Lamar" width="298" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mirabeaulamar.jpg: Unknown authorUnknown author derivative work: Oldag07 (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirabeaulamar_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
